@*
    What a list is, and what is chosen in it, over the list itself.

    The same line a tab carries, for the arrangement that has no tabs. Where there is room for both
    lists at once there is nothing to switch between, so each column says what it is above itself
    instead - which is what these strips were before they became tabs.

    Only one of the two is ever in the page: the container query hides whichever does not apply, and
    a hidden element is out of the accessibility tree as well as off the screen. So a reader is never
    offered a tab to a list that is already open beside it, and never a heading with no list under it.
*@

<div class="head">
    <span class="title">@Tab.Title</span>
    <span class="state">@Tab.State</span>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public required PickerTabs.Tab Tab { get; set; }
}
